## Conventions & gotchas

- **Versioning is git-tag-derived** (`hatch-vcs`). Never hand-edit a version; `src/[[ package_name ]]/_version.py` is generated (gitignored). Tag `vX.Y.Z` to release.
- **`src/` layout, `py.typed`, Pydantic v2, `structlog`.** Ruff line-length 120; keep it clean (`make lint`) before committing.
[% if has_server %]- **Any endpoint that does something is a boundary.** There's no auth by default — treat reaching the port as host access. Gate state-changing routes behind the shared read-only / origin guards, and fence any caller-supplied path under a configured root.
[% endif %]- Wire schemas (if any) are checked in and verified in CI — regenerate and commit when the types change, don't let the committed copy drift.

## Branches

`dev` is the default branch and the base for every PR. Cut feature branches from `origin/dev` and bring them up to date by merging `origin/dev`, never `main`. Never push work to `main` or open a PR against it, except the release PR from `dev`: `main` must never be ahead of `dev`, with one exception. A release fast-forwards `main` to a `dev` commit that passed CI (`git push origin origin/dev:main`), then tags it. If `main` is protected, the release is a reviewed PR from `dev` into `main`, and merging it leaves a merge commit on `main` alone. That merge commit is the one exception to the rule: it leaves `main` one commit ahead of `dev` with an identical tree. Leave it there and don't merge `main` back into `dev`. Anything else on `main` that `dev` lacks is a mistake (`git diff origin/dev origin/main` must be empty). Once `main` carries such a commit it can't be fast-forwarded, so later releases are PRs too.

## CI / release

CI runs via the shared [`argus-ci`](https://github.com/[[ github_owner ]]/argus-ci) reusable workflow. `docs.yml` runs its `docs-check` on every push: published docs (`README.md`, `docs/**/*.md`) must hold no private IPs, home/server paths or personal emails (use placeholders like `<GPU_HOST>`)[% if has_cli %], and `docs/cli.md` must match the CLI — run `make docs` after changing a command[% endif %]. Release publishes to PyPI (OIDC trusted publishing) + GHCR on `v*` tags. Run `copier update` to pull template (CI/release/tooling) changes.
